 Guidelines for contributors working on this repository.
 
+## Phase-Gated Testing
+
+Tests are a certification gate, not a continuous implementation activity.
+During an implementation phase, write or update tests as needed, but do not
+execute automated suites or manual test flows. Static inspection and cohesive
+non-test compile or type checks may run when needed. Only after every
+implementation task in the phase is complete, run the applicable tests once as
+a consolidated gate immediately before reflection. If the gate fails, return to
+implementation, batch related fixes, and rerun tests only when the phase is
+complete again. Never test after individual tasks or continuously.
+
 ## Commit Conventions
 
 Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):
